From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] exec: room for a task's instruction count, not only its time

iet_CpuUsage is a share of wall clock, which is the only thing a machine
with a cycle counter can measure. A machine whose CPU is translated can
measure something else: how many guest instructions a task actually
executed. The two disagree whenever some code runs or translates more
cheaply than other code -- a task busy on MMIO and a task busy on
register arithmetic do very different amounts of m68k work per second.

Three fields, at the end of the structure and next to the sample state
they mirror. Every target that cannot count instructions leaves them
zero, which is what they already read.

arch/m68k-emu68 fills them from Emu68's INSNCNT control register.
---
diff --git a/rom/exec/etask.h b/rom/exec/etask.h
index c44955392b..fbeef1352e 100644
--- a/rom/exec/etask.h
+++ b/rom/exec/etask.h
@@ -66,6 +66,16 @@ struct IntETask
     /* Last CPU-usage sample, for arches that sweep iet_CpuUsage. */
     UQUAD               iet_LastBusy;           /* iet_private2 at the last sample         */
     UQUAD               iet_LastUsageStamp;     /* when that sample was taken              */
+    /*
+     * Guest work done, for a target that runs the CPU under a translator and
+     * can count its instructions. iet_CpuUsage is a share of wall clock; this
+     * is a share of instructions actually executed, which is not the same
+     * number whenever some code translates or runs more cheaply than other
+     * code. Left at zero by every target that cannot count them.
+     */
+    UQUAD               iet_CpuInsn;            /* instructions this task has executed     */
+    UQUAD               iet_LastInsn;           /* iet_CpuInsn at the last sample          */
+    ULONG               iet_InsnUsage;          /* share of instructions, 0..0xffffffff    */
     ULONG               iet_QuantumLeft;        /* scheduler ticks left of this task's slice */
 #ifdef DEBUG_ETASK
     STRPTR              iet_Me;
